    "q-252987": {
      "dom_id": "step-q252987",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "What is the supremum of the set $A=\\{-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2\\}?$\n\n$sup(A)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The supremum of a set $A$ is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nIf $A$ is a finite set, the supremum of $A$ equals its maximum. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sup(A) & =max\\{-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2\\}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
